    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0597" n="527" xml:id="pg527"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Tassara.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 9, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, Secretary of State of the United States, has the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of Mr. Tassara’s note, of the 23d ultimo, in
                    continuation of previous notes on the subject of the conduct of United States
                    cruisers on the coast of Cuba, and, in reply, to inform him that a copy of it
                    has been communicated to the Secretary of the Navy, whose instructions in the
                    premises to United States naval commanders in the Gulf, Mr. Tassara may rest
                    assured, will be as liberal as the public safety may permit, and always
                    consistent with public law.</p>
                <p>The undersigned offers to Mr. Tassara renewed assurances of his high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Sénor <hi rendition="#small-caps">Don Gabriel Garcia y Tassara</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
